            "content": "{\"tools\":[{\"name\":\"save_code_skill\",\"description\":\"Save a code skill (SKILL.md with scripts/run.ts or scripts/run.sh) for run_skill to run. The app keeps it for this conversation: its runs, and the cards and verifiers of its Goal, can run it; a review later decides whether the project's other conversations get it. Make each skill one purpose-specific job, reuse a listed skill when one fits, and do not wrap a single tool call. A ts skill is a program that calls your tools as functions, as in run_code, with the input it declares. A sh skill is a script, the only way to run host commands: it runs sandboxed, writes only inside the project, temp folders and package caches, cannot read credential folders or the app's storage, and reaches only the hosts in network. Saving asks for approval of the exact program and host list; later runs of the unchanged program, with any input or arguments, do not ask. Saving under an existing skill's name replaces it for this conversation. Read the code-skill-writing skill before the first save in a conversation.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"maxLength\":64,\"description\":\"Skill name: lowercase words joined by hyphens, naming the job (e.g. test-failures, package-exports).\"},\"description\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"description\":\"One line on what the skill does and when to use it; it is listed so later runs can find it.\"},\"program\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"runtime\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"ts\"]},\"code\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"description\":\"TypeScript for one job: the body of an async function that reads `input`, calls tools as `await external_<tool name>(input)` and returns a small JSON value.\"},\"input\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"description\":\"JSON Schema of `input`, of type \\\"object\\\"; every run is checked against it. Omit when the skill takes no input.\"}},\"required\":[